---
date: 2025-06-16T00:00:00-04:00
---

Star 221,325 is a [[Joker World]] 221,325 worlds starward of Færrin prime. A [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] scouting party found it while searching the [[Infinite Horizon]] for places of interest, drawn by a magical presence and by slip-shielding over part of the surface.

An indigo rain falls here without pause. Where Færrin prime would show grassland south of Calaria, the ground is broken into leaning plateaus and canyons, and the rain soaks in rather than flooding, leaving the footing soft and slow. Toward the middle of a wide crater the plateaus tilt inward, and greenish-blue fire shows there, the only steady light under the rain. Lines run across the canyon walls where falling rain hisses away the moment it lands. The lines have no visible source and grow denser nearer the center. The cracks are where the world's creatures come from: [[Hellion|Hellions]] climb out of them by the horde. One climber put a hand on a crack that split open in his face, blasting him with sulfurous steam while a small trident jabbed out of the fire at his neck.

At the center stands a sealed structure built of some combination of metal and vine. It has a single door. When the scouting party tried the door, the structure asked them a question, and the head of the party was frightened enough to send for help. Some of the party had already died crossing the chasms, and none of them were found afterward.

The Scale sent four delving specialists to finish the work. Walking the last mile of the canyons, three of them heard a thought in their own voice, asking whether the work was worth it and how far they were willing to go. The fourth heard nothing.

Cliff Vandertrip, Manuel de la Cruzada, Zangron Lee and Gregor fought their way through hordes of Hellions that poured up out of the cracks, and at last reached the structure. Its door shaped a question out of metal and vine, asking whether they would descend to save a soul tormented by captors, and swung open when all four answered yes. The building within is [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]].
